# Install

<p class="lede">One command installs the Atmos host: a local Sepolia RPC endpoint for your wallet, whose calls leave through the Nym mixnet and whose reads are checked against a light client.</p>

<CopyLine text="curl -fsSL https://atmos.xavio.dev/install.sh | sh" />

## Requirements

- Linux or macOS, with `git`, `npm` and **Node 24 or newer**.
- `systemctl`, only if you want the host to run in the background.

## What it does

1. Clones the parts of the repository the host needs (`client`, `sdk`, `harness`, `host`) into `~/.atmos`. Run again, it updates that copy.
2. Builds the Node harness and the host with `npm ci`, from the committed lockfiles.
3. Writes a launcher, `~/.atmos/atmos-host`.
4. Asks whether to install a systemd user service, so the host runs in the background. It writes nothing outside `~/.atmos` unless you agree.

The host picks its own trust anchor: the finalized beacon block root two beacon APIs agree on, fetched through the mixnet. Set `ATMOS_CHECKPOINT` to use your own.

## Add it to MetaMask

In MetaMask, open Settings, then Networks, then Add a network manually:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Network name | Sepolia via Atmos |
| RPC URL | `http://127.0.0.1:8545/11155111` |
| Chain ID | `11155111` |
| Currency symbol | SepoliaETH |

<CopyLine text="http://127.0.0.1:8545/11155111" />

The first answer takes 15 to 70 seconds while the host joins the mixnet. `http://127.0.0.1:8545/` shows whether it is ready and counts its answers by kind.

## Settings

Set these in the environment of the install command, for example `curl -fsSL https://atmos.xavio.dev/install.sh | ATMOS_PORT=8546 sh`.

| Variable | Default | What it sets |
|---|---|---|
| `ATMOS_DIR` | `~/.atmos` | Install directory |
| `ATMOS_PORT` | `8545` | Local port |
| `ATMOS_SERVICE` | ask | `1` installs the systemd user service, `0` doesn't |
| `ATMOS_CHECKPOINT` | chosen by the host | A trusted Sepolia beacon block root |
| `ATMOS_REPO` | the Atmos repository | Git URL to install from |
| `ATMOS_REF` | `main` | Branch or tag |

## Run and stop it

Without the service, start the host with `~/.atmos/atmos-host`. With it:

```sh
journalctl --user -u atmos-host -f        # logs
systemctl --user stop atmos-host          # stop
```

## Remove it

```sh
systemctl --user disable --now atmos-host        # if you installed the service
rm ~/.config/systemd/user/atmos-host.service     # if you installed the service
rm -rf ~/.atmos
```

## Other ways in

- **In your own app:** the [SDK](/docs/sdk/) gives you the same verified, mixnet-routed calls as an EIP-1193 provider.
- **Docker, or a host for others:** [Self-host](/docs/self-host/) covers the Docker images, the browser runtime, access rules and the constant-rate schedule.
